{
  "info": {
    "name": "Legacy Platform MCP — Tool Calls",
    "description": "Calls the MCP server's tools over raw JSON-RPC, the way a gateway does.\n\nWhy requests 01 and 02 exist: the MCP streamable-HTTP transport requires a handshake. `initialize` returns an `mcp-session-id` response header, and every later request must echo it back — calling a tool without one returns `400 Bad Request: Missing session ID`. Request 01 captures that header into {{mcpSessionId}} automatically; a collection-level pre-request script attaches it to everything after.\n\nSo: run 01, then 02, then any tool request. Or just use Run Collection, which does them in order.\n\nThis collection plays the gateway's role by injecting `Authorization: Basic` itself (set at collection level from the {{username}}/{{password}} variables). That is exactly what the server expects the Bridge to do.\n\nResponses come back as Server-Sent Events, so the body looks like `event: message\\ndata: {...}`. A collection-level test script parses the JSON out of that and stores it in {{lastResult}}, and prints the tool's own payload to the Postman Console (View > Show Postman Console) where it is far easier to read.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "mcpUrl",
      "value": "https://api-basic-auth-mcp.onrender.com/mcp",
      "type": "string"
    },
    { "key": "username", "value": "svc_agent", "type": "string" },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "q3Fnt4Ak0p1jDNs0OXQGEz6awpxbK8f-",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "readerUsername",
      "value": "analyst",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Reader-role identity, for demonstrating the authorization difference."
    },
    {
      "key": "readerPassword",
      "value": "Kzg8vC7Ww_AW0h3cKpQX0LABHNcmivbm",
      "type": "string"
    },
    { "key": "mcpSessionId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accountId", "value": "ACCT-1001", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "lastResult", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "basic",
    "basic": [
      { "key": "username", "value": "{{username}}", "type": "string" },
      { "key": "password", "value": "{{password}}", "type": "string" }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Attach the MCP session id to every request except initialize.",
          "// Without it the server replies 400 'Missing session ID'.",
          "const name = pm.info.requestName || '';",
          "if (!name.startsWith('01')) {",
          "  const sid = pm.collectionVariables.get('mcpSessionId');",
          "  if (!sid) {",
          "    console.warn('No mcpSessionId yet — run \"01 — initialize\" first.');",
          "  } else {",
          "    pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'mcp-session-id', value: sid });",
          "  }",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// MCP replies as SSE: 'event: message\\ndata: {json}'. Pull out the JSON.",
          "function parseRpc(raw) {",
          "  if (!raw) return null;",
          "  for (const line of raw.split('\\n')) {",
          "    const t = line.trim();",
          "    const body = t.startsWith('data:') ? t.slice(5).trim() : t;",
          "    if (body.startsWith('{')) {",
          "      try { return JSON.parse(body); } catch (e) { /* keep looking */ }",
          "    }",
          "  }",
          "  return null;",
          "}",
          "",
          "const rpc = parseRpc(pm.response.text());",
          "if (rpc) {",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('lastResult', JSON.stringify(rpc));",
          "",
          "  pm.test('JSON-RPC response carries no error', function () {",
          "    pm.expect(rpc.error, rpc.error && rpc.error.message).to.be.undefined;",
          "  });",
          "",
          "  // A tool result arrives as content[0].text holding the tool's JSON.",
          "  const content = rpc.result && rpc.result.content;",
          "  if (content && content.length && content[0].type === 'text') {",
          "    let payload;",
          "    try { payload = JSON.parse(content[0].text); } catch (e) { payload = content[0].text; }",
          "    console.log(pm.info.requestName, '->', payload);",
          "",
          "    if (payload && typeof payload === 'object' && 'success' in payload) {",
          "      // Requests named '(expect failure)' are asserting the error path.",
          "      const wantsFailure = /expect failure/i.test(pm.info.requestName);",
          "      pm.test(wantsFailure ? 'tool reports failure, as expected' : 'tool reports success', function () {",
          "        pm.expect(payload.success).to.eql(!wantsFailure);",
          "      });",
          "      if (wantsFailure) {",
          "        pm.test('failure includes an explanation', function () {",
          "          pm.expect(payload.error, 'no error message').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
          "        });",
          "      }",
          "    }",
          "  }",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 — initialize (run this first)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"initialize\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"protocolVersion\": \"2024-11-05\",\n    \"capabilities\": {},\n    \"clientInfo\": { \"name\": \"postman\", \"version\": \"1.0\" }\n  }\n}"
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{mcpUrl}}", "host": ["{{mcpUrl}}"] },
        "description": "Opens the MCP session. The `mcp-session-id` RESPONSE header is captured into {{mcpSessionId}} and reused by every later request.\n\nIf a tool request returns `400 Missing session ID`, the session has expired or the server restarted — re-run this request."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const sid = pm.response.headers.get('mcp-session-id');",
              "pm.test('server returned an mcp-session-id header', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(sid, 'header absent').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "});",
              "if (sid) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('mcpSessionId', sid);",
              "  console.log('Captured mcp-session-id:', sid);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 — notifications/initialized",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"method\": \"notifications/initialized\"\n}"
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{mcpUrl}}", "host": ["{{mcpUrl}}"] },
        "description": "Completes the handshake. This is a notification, so there is no response body and the server replies 202 Accepted."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('202 Accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(202));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 — tools/list",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 2,\n  \"method\": \"tools/list\"\n}"
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{mcpUrl}}", "host": ["{{mcpUrl}}"] },
        "description": "Lists the seven tools with their input schemas. This is what an agent reads to decide what it can call."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const raw = pm.response.text();",
              "let rpc = null;",
              "for (const line of raw.split('\\n')) {",
              "  const t = line.trim();",
              "  const b = t.startsWith('data:') ? t.slice(5).trim() : t;",
              "  if (b.startsWith('{')) { try { rpc = JSON.parse(b); break; } catch (e) {} }",
              "}",
              "pm.test('returned a tool list', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(rpc && rpc.result && rpc.result.tools).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
              "});",
              "if (rpc && rpc.result && rpc.result.tools) {",
              "  const names = rpc.result.tools.map(t => t.name);",
              "  console.log('Tools:', names.join(', '));",
              "  pm.test('all 7 tools present', () => pm.expect(names).to.have.lengthOf(7));",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "04 — credential_source (is injection working?)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 3,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"credential_source\",\n    \"arguments\": {}\n  }\n}"
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{mcpUrl}}", "host": ["{{mcpUrl}}"] },
        "description": "The diagnostic to reach for first. Reports the auth scheme and username the server received, never the password.\n\nWorking:        auth_scheme \"Basic\", username \"svc_agent\"\nGateway broken: auth_scheme \"Bearer\", username null — the gateway is relaying the agent's token instead of exchanging it for the vaulted credential."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const r = JSON.parse(pm.collectionVariables.get('lastResult') || '{}');",
              "const c = r.result && r.result.content;",
              "if (c && c.length) {",
              "  const p = JSON.parse(c[0].text);",
              "  pm.test('credential arrived as Basic', () => pm.expect(p.auth_scheme).to.eql('Basic'));",
              "  pm.test('server stores no credentials of its own', () => pm.expect(p.holds_stored_credentials).to.be.false);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "05 — platform_health (no credential needed)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json, text/event-stream" }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 4,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"platform_health\",\n    \"arguments\": {}\n  }\n}"
        },
        "url": { "raw": "{{mcpUrl}}", "host": ["{{mcpUrl}}"] },
        "description": "Reachability check that needs no credential. Call it first after an idle period: both Render free-tier services sleep, and this wakes the platform without burning a credentialed call on a 60-second timeout."
      }
    },
